15:09.800 --> 15:13.760
With Utah County, I would probably do somewhere close

15:14.260 --> 15:18.300
to, with expenses, $60,000 to $80,000 each

15:18.800 --> 15:21.760
year. Okay. Outside of the ARPA work that we're doing,

15:22.260 --> 15:26.380
because we have some other rules with them, we do some other federal consulting

15:26.880 --> 15:30.060
work with them. With Eagle Mountain City,

15:30.560 --> 15:34.705
it depends on You know, the tasks that I'm

15:34.801 --> 15:38.408
asked to do, and if I'm training someone, I am— I'm close

15:38.488 --> 15:41.518
enough to retirement that I'm not a long-term solution.

15:42.047 --> 15:45.349
So, you know, and I'm aware of that, and I want

15:45.849 --> 15:49.421
to be very clear about that. I'm not— I'm not a 5-year,

15:49.646 --> 15:53.541
10-year solution. No. I'm a short-term, couple of years,

15:54.295 --> 15:57.709
getting something up and running, training someone.

15:57.960 --> 16:01.770
And I'm retiring. Got it.

16:02.270 --> 16:06.110
That's awesome. Well, I work in the retirement industry, so anytime someone

16:06.610 --> 16:10.450
moves into retirement, I love it. Yeah. Well, well deserved.

16:10.830 --> 16:14.570
So is our load about equivalent to Utah County,

16:15.070 --> 16:19.890
would you say? No. Okay. So we might anticipate $30,000

16:20.390 --> 16:23.490
to $40,000 a year, something like that. Okay. Thank you.

16:23.990 --> 16:26.850
That's, that's kind of what I just wanted to wrap my arms around. Thank you.

16:27.350 --> 16:31.490
Can I actually— I'll submit detailed timesheets for billings

16:31.990 --> 16:36.320
because that's required by 2 CFR 200 federal regulation.

16:36.770 --> 16:39.970
And I do those trainings around the country too.

16:40.470 --> 16:43.850
So I'll submit detailed timesheets. You'll know what I'm doing. Okay. No, no.

16:44.350 --> 16:47.640
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, for sure. And then just going— thank you, Elizabeth.

16:48.850 --> 16:52.490
And then maybe just my last question for, for Kiara.

16:52.990 --> 16:56.427
Is this something that You feel like we should

16:56.927 --> 16:59.287
have somebody part-time doing this?

17:00.123 --> 17:03.899
I feel like if we hired somebody part-time, it would be about the same cost

17:04.236 --> 17:08.815
as what we're paying to Elizabeth to kind of manage the program.

17:10.165 --> 17:13.459
Or I guess this

17:13.959 --> 17:17.942
is just like a training opportunity, or are there more things

17:18.199 --> 17:21.826
off of your plate that need to be lifted? I think,

17:22.853 --> 17:26.092
and it's kind of hard to say because it depends on how we,

17:26.781 --> 17:30.694
you know, execute our projects really. If they were all going externally,

17:30.967 --> 17:34.800
and I'm not making a recommendation, I'm just saying if they go externally,

17:34.816 --> 17:39.467
that heavy lift is more so on the organization versus

17:39.967 --> 17:43.139
if we have internal projects like ADA ramps and different things like that,

17:43.155 --> 17:45.929
that requires more internal tracking and compliance.

17:47.330 --> 17:50.910
efforts. Um, and so that doesn't really answer the question. In a

17:51.410 --> 17:54.670
